  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Chef Viktor is angry because Senya and Fedya got fired. He reassigns their names to the remaining cooks in the kitchen. Let's listen closely to their exchange in Russian first, and then walk through each line together.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Сеня, соус готов?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "artyom",
      "t": "А я не Сеня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "artyom",
      "t": "Я Артем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Сеню уволили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Мне плевать, кто ты.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Сегодня ты Сеня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Федя бы это быстро сделал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Я тоже Федя, шеф.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Нет, ты не Федя.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Имя Федя заслужить надо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Теперь ты Артем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Да, шеф.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through the exchange around New names line by line and unpack how the Russian works.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Сеня, соус готов?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Senya, is the sauce ready?' Barinov barks an order about the sauce, aggressively addressing his cook by the wrong name.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "artyom",
      "t": "А я не Сеня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am not Senya.' Artyom tentatively corrects his boss, dropping the verb 'to be' as is standard in Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "artyom",
      "t": "Я Артем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am Artyom.' Artyom states his actual name simply and directly, omitting the present-tense verb.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Сеню уволили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Senya got fired.' Barinov dismisses the correction, bluntly stating that the real Senya was just fired.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Мне плевать, кто ты.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I do not care who you are.' Barinov aggressively declares his indifference to his employee's true identity.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Сегодня ты Сеня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Today you are Senya.' Barinov forces the new name upon him for the day, connecting the words directly without a verb.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Федя бы это быстро сделал.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Fedya would have done it fast.' Barinov complains about the slow pace by comparing another cook to the recently fired Fedya.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Я тоже Федя, шеф.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am Fedya too, Chef.' Fedya chimes in to say that he is also named Fedya, pointing out the coincidence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Нет, ты не Федя.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'No, you are not Fedya.' Barinov instantly strips him of his real name, aggressively denying his identity.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Имя Федя заслужить надо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You have to earn the name Fedya.' Barinov absurdly elevates the name to a title of honor that must be earned through hard work.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Теперь ты Артем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Now you are Artyom.' Barinov reassigns the name Artyom to him, treating his staff completely interchangeably.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Да, шеф.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, Chef.' — Built around the key proper name meaning 'chef, boss'. Now listen to the whole scene again. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
